Prove fresh human membership through a deployed Receiving HTTP route

Usage: wamn-gates membershipproof [OPTIONS] --system-database-url <SYSTEM_DATABASE_URL> --project-database-url <PROJECT_DATABASE_URL> --endpoint-url <ENDPOINT_URL> --host <HOST> --org <ORG> --project <PROJECT> --env <ENV> --tenant <TENANT>

Options:
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Log level (the Jobs pass this before the subcommand) [default: info]
      --system-database-url <SYSTEM_DATABASE_URL>
          Provisioning administrator URL for the existing system database [env: WAMN_SYSTEM_ADMIN_URL]
      --project-database-url <PROJECT_DATABASE_URL>
          Administrator URL for the existing Receiving project database [env: WAMN_PROJECT_ADMIN_URL]
      --endpoint-url <ENDPOINT_URL>
          Reachable base URL of the deployed Receiving route
      --host <HOST>
          Released route's HTTP Host header
      --org <ORG>
          Organization that owns the disposable fixture
      --project <PROJECT>
          Project that owns the disposable fixture
      --env <ENV>
          Exact provisioned environment
      --tenant <TENANT>
          Tenant already attached to the released route
      --throughput-pat-file <THROUGHPUT_PAT_FILE>
          Seed a disposable human benchmark fixture and write its PAT to a new mode-0600 file. The journey teardown owns these retained facts; this mode runs no HTTP proof
  -h, --help
          Print help
